Original iOS log on no-PR: `'ℹ️ No open feature PR found — triggering on develop'` — printed when `!featurePrUrl` (even when pr found with EMPTY url? pr found → url could be '' if both html_url and url missing → then prints the no-PR message). Mine: `if (pr) {...} else {log}` — if pr found with url '' → NO log (differs!). Edge: pr matched but no url — original logs 'no open feature PR' anyway. Fix: match original exactly: `if (!pr || !pr.url) { log no-pr }` hmm — but then `result.branch = pr.branch || result.branch` still runs when pr matched... Original:
