```js
if (!pr || !pr.url) console.log(no-pr); 
if (pr) { branch, url assignments }
```
CC: 1 base + catch 1 + !(owner&&repo) 2 + `!pr || !pr.url` 2 + `pr.branch || result.branch` 1 = 7 ✓ OK. Reorder: log first (matches original order: found-log inside find, then no-pr log after loop) ✓.

Same TA issue? TA original: after PR loop `if (!featurePrUrl) { console.log('ℹ️ No open feature PR found for', ticketKey, '— will run automation anyway'); }`. My searchFeaturePr: `if (!pr.url) log` — but when owner/repo missing → no log at all (original: the whole block skipped → no log ✓). And when findFeaturePr returns {url:''} → log ✓. When pr matched with url? no log ✓. When listPrs throws → catch ✓ (original: catch wraps whole block ✓). TA case ✓ — because `if (!pr.url)` covers both "no pr found" and "pr without url" ✓ matches original.

