Wait — a behavioural bug in my iOS refactor: `resolveIosTicket` guard. Original:

```js
if (inputJql) { ... ticket fetch ... }
if (!ticketKey) { error }
```

When inputJql empty → skip fetch → error 'No ticket found for: ' (empty jql) ✓ mine: resolveIosTicket('') → {key:''} → error ✓.

Another: `parseTriggerResult` — original logs '✅ Bitrise build triggered: build #' + (buildData.build_number || '?') AFTER parse. Mine: parse → log inside ✓.

But one real difference: iOS original comment built AFTER parseTriggerResult even if... ✓ same.

`resolveIosFeatureBranch`: original sets `branch = prBranch || branch` where prBranch could be '' → keeps 'develop' ✓ mine `result.branch = pr.branch || result.branch`.

Original iOS log on no-PR: `'ℹ️ No open feature PR found — triggering on develop'` — printed when `!featurePrUrl` (even when pr found with EMPTY url? pr found → url could be '' if both html_url and url missing → then prints the no-PR message). Mine: `if (pr) {...} else {log}` — if pr found with url '' → NO log (differs!). Edge: pr matched but no url — original logs 'no open feature PR' anyway. Fix: match original exactly: `if (!pr || !pr.url) { log no-pr }` hmm — but then `result.branch = pr.branch || result.branch` still runs when pr matched... Original:
```js
if (prTitle matches) {
    branch = prBranch || branch;
    featurePrUrl = pr.html_url || pr.url || '';
    log found
    break;
}
...
if (!featurePrUrl) { log no-PR }
```
So: pr matched w/o url → 'found' logged AND 'no-PR' logged. pr not matched → only 'no-PR'. Fix my helper:

```js
var pr = findFeaturePrWithBranch(...);
if (pr) {
    result.branch = pr.branch || result.branch;
    result.url = pr.url;
    if (!pr.url) console.log('ℹ️ No open feature PR found — triggering on develop');
} else {
    console.log('ℹ️ No open feature PR found — triggering on develop');
}
```
That adds CC. Alternative: make findFeaturePrWithBranch return null when url empty? NO — original still uses prBranch (branch!) even when url empty. Hmm: pr matched, head.ref 'ai/X', no urls → branch='ai/X', featurePrUrl='' → BOTH logs. My resolveIosFeatureBranch: 
```js
if (!pr || !pr.url) console.log(no-pr); 
if (pr) { branch, url assignments }
```
CC: 1 base + catch 1 + !(owner&&repo) 2 + `!pr || !pr.url` 2 + `pr.branch || result.branch` 1 = 7 ✓ OK. Reorder: log first (matches original order: found-log inside find, then no-pr log after loop) ✓.

Same TA issue? TA original: after PR loop `if (!featurePrUrl) { console.log('ℹ️ No open feature PR found for', ticketKey, '— will run automation anyway'); }`. My searchFeaturePr: `if (!pr.url) log` — but when owner/repo missing → no log at all (original: the whole block skipped → no log ✓). And when findFeaturePr returns {url:''} → log ✓. When pr matched with url? no log ✓. When listPrs throws → catch ✓ (original: catch wraps whole block ✓). TA case ✓ — because `if (!pr.url)` covers both "no pr found" and "pr without url" ✓ matches original.

For iOS fix — let me patch resolveIosFeatureBranch.

